# Helium Rapid DSL MCP Server - Cursor Rules

This folder (`helium-rapid-dsl-mcp/`) contains an MCP server used by Cursor agents when generating/editing Helium Rapid DSL:
- `.mez` (Helium Rapid DSL (ANTLR4))
- `.vxml` (Helium UI views)

## Core intent

- This MCP server exists to expose **AST/LSP-style** capabilities to AI agents (validate, navigate, refactor preview), not to “guess” DSL structure.
- Prefer using the Helium language server’s AST/index for `.mez` rather than duplicating logic.

## Entry point (critical)

- The compiled MCP entrypoint is:
  - `out/src/index.js`
- Do NOT configure Cursor to run `out/index.js` (it will not exist with the current build layout).

## Bundled in VSIX (Cursor)

- When packaged, the MCP server is bundled inside the extension:
  - `helium-dsl-vscode/server/mcp/out/src/index.js`
- The extension registers the MCP server via `mcpServerDefinitionProviders`, so Cursor users can enable it directly from **MCP: List Servers**.

## Node ESM learnings (Cursor runtime)

Cursor may launch MCP servers using a strict Node ESM runtime (e.g. Node 25). In that environment:

- **Always use explicit `.js` import suffixes** when required by the dependency’s ESM exports.
  - Good: `vscode-languageserver/node.js`
  - Bad: `vscode-languageserver/node`
  - Good: `antlr4ts/tree/ParseTreeWalker.js`
  - Bad: `antlr4ts/tree/ParseTreeWalker`

If you add new imports in `helium-dsl-language-server`, prefer `.js` suffixed specifiers to prevent MCP startup failures.

## Dependency coupling rules

- Prefer importing from `helium-dsl-language-server/api` (stable public surface) rather than deep imports into `out/src/**`.
- If you change the language server build output paths, also update its `package.json` `exports` map.

## VXML validation rules

- Validate:
  - `view@unit` exists as a `.mez` unit
  - `view@init`, `action@action`, `collectionSource@function`, `visible@function` exist in the unit
  - bound variables exist (`binding@variable`, `visible@variable`, etc.)
  - model attribute names exist on the bound object type where resolvable
  - enum values referenced by `<enum>` exist
  - language keys exist across **all** `web-app/lang/*.lang` files

## Generated files

- Do not edit any generated files under `helium-vscode-tooling/generated/**` or compiled outputs under `out/**`.
- Make source changes in `src/**` and regenerate via build scripts.

